comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-13T03:07:33.477Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1717 CodeRabbit (major), fixed in this PR: pm plan create, add-step and update-step assigned --step-owner without the identity refusal, so a plan step owner could still store URL userinfo through the plan commands even after the declared table judged plan_steps owner in create metadata and runtime field values. All three paths now go through resolveStepOwner, which refuses URL userinfo with invalid_argument_value naming --step-owner and keeps the trim-and-blank-clears behaviour; plan-command spec covers the three paths and a plain owner.\n"
